/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 956 0 R
/ActualText (This study evaluates electrification and performs a techno-economic analysis of hybrid systems for rural communities in Rivers State. The optimal choice, based on hourly electricity demand, is a grid/PV module combination. The proposed systems have a lower cost of energy \(COE\) compared to the grid, and the research includes a sensitivity analysis to guide decision-making and system design.[3])
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
391 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 957 0 R
/ActualText ( The Aluu, Choba and Rumuekini communities experienced an average daily electricity supply of 4.6, 5.4 and 6.2 h respectively from the national grid with energy usage of 5436.4 MW for Aluu, 3375.4 MW for Choba and 1626.1 MW for Rumuekini, in 2022. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [1]
