401 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 959 0 R
/ActualText (The study focuses on the issues of hydrogen energy storage which can solve the fluctuating output power problem by simulating results on HOMER software. Three combinations of the Solar-Hydrogen system, Wind-Hydrogen system, and Solar-Wind-Hydrogen hybrid system are presented to find the most optimum one. Levelized Cost of Energy \(LCOE\) for Hybrid System has proven to be the most economical while the Wind Turbine cost 1.476% higher and the Solar Photovoltaics \(PV\) System costs 108.03% more. LCOE for Hybrid Model is $0.3387, while for Solar System it is $ 0.7046 and for Wind System it is $ 0.3437. These results show that a hydrogen-based energy storage system is viable for the considered.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
402 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 960 0 R
/ActualText (Main purpose of the system is the electricity supply of a residential community and hydrogen production to stabilize the intermittency of renewable energy sources. Simulations were done using HOMER software for power stations energized by Solar-Hydrogen storage, Wind-Hydrogen storage, and Wind and Solar Hybrid-Hydrogen storage power system,  The software HOMER is used to detect the most feasible electrical load component sizes.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
